wayland: do not try to connect when no compositor socket can be named.

SDL tries its Wayland driver first. Run full screen from the console (psh),
where there is no Wayland session, Wayland_CreateDevice() still calls
wl_display_connect(NULL); with WAYLAND_DISPLAY, WAYLAND_SOCKET and
XDG_RUNTIME_DIR all unset that call cannot succeed, and libwayland prints
"error: XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is invalid or not set in the environment." before
failing, so every game started from psh logged it. SDL then fell through to
KMSDRM as intended.

Return NULL before the connect in exactly that case. It is the case where
libwayland's connect_to_socket() gives up (a relative default "wayland-0" and no
runtime dir), so the outcome is unchanged -- only the line is gone. A desktop
client (labwc exports WAYLAND_DISPLAY; game-window.sh exports XDG_RUNTIME_DIR)
takes the unchanged path.

--- a/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandvideo.c
+++ b/src/video/wayland/SDL_waylandvideo.c
@@ -183,6 +183,16 @@
         }
     }
 
+    /* No compositor socket can be named: with none of WAYLAND_DISPLAY,
+       WAYLAND_SOCKET or XDG_RUNTIME_DIR set, wl_display_connect() can only fail,
+       and it prints "error: XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is invalid or not set in the
+       environment." on the way. Skip the attempt quietly, so that a program run
+       outside a Wayland session (full screen from a console) falls through to the
+       next video driver without that line. */
+    if (!getenv("WAYLAND_DISPLAY") && !getenv("WAYLAND_SOCKET") && !getenv("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR")) {
+        return NULL;
+    }
+
     if (!SDL_WAYLAND_LoadSymbols()) {
         return NULL;
     }
